md=['# RouterBSI — independent presentation, figure and compliance audit','',f"**Review target:** `source/main.pdf`, SHA-256 `{physical['pdf_sha256']}`.",'','**Outcome:** 31 total pages, **8 content-bearing pages**, all **8 figures** and all **31 pages** checked. Main prose concludes on p7, but Figures 5–7 continue on p8 before Limitations. No manuscript edits or experiments. Source snapshot hashes verified unchanged.','', '## Internal scores (1–5, not official ARR ratings)','', '| Dimension | Score | Rationale |','|---|---:|---|']
for k in ['presentation','figure_quality','narrative','confidence']:
    x=report['internal_scores'][k];md.append(f"| {k.replace('_',' ').title()} | {x['score']} | {x['justification']} |")
md+=['','Scientific soundness/contribution and an acceptance recommendation are outside this focused audit. Official ARR scales remain unverified.','','## Physical facts versus venue obligations','','- **Physical facts:** every page is A4 (595.276 × 841.890 pt); two-column prose, ACL review class/options, page numbers and prose review rulers are present. All font records are embedded according to `pdffonts`, including Type 3. Searchable text is present on every page; no text span lies outside its page box. Rendered pages show no gross overlap or clipping.','- **Page boundary:** conclusion p7; body Figures 5–7 p8; Limitations starts p8 left column at y≈687 pt and continues into the right column; ethics and AI-only acknowledgment follow; References pp8–11; appendices A–H pp11–31. Wide tables on float-only pp29–31 are not single-column appendix prose.','- **Conditional page assessment:** fits the assumed long-review 8-page limit, with zero whole pages spare. Actual venue, cycle, stage, paper type and PDF-upload permission are unknown; no unconditional submission-compliance claim.','- **Anonymity/disclosure:** anonymous byline/metadata, no obvious PDF identity leak. Fresh `policy/3.txt` explicitly permits AI-only acknowledgments. The existing p8 disclosure is therefore **not** an anonymity violation. Current CFP asks for scope in the Responsible NLP Checklist and details in acknowledgments; actual use and form completeness remain human checks.','- **Limitations/ethics:** both occur before references; no new results or figures appear inside Limitations. Ethics discusses medical non-validity, untrusted execution, licenses and sensitive external-service data. This does not establish actual license/privacy compliance.','- **Unverified:** official style-file provenance, submission-form/checklist fields, supplements, author approval/profiles, reviewer obligations, eligibility, overlap/prior submission and preprint status. Do not infer these from the PDF.','- **Abstract:** 200 whitespace-delimited words in source; no abstract-length finding. PDF title metadata omits “Replay” from the printed title, a minor metadata synchronization note, not an anonymity issue.','','## Prioritized findings','']
for x in issues:
    a=x['location'];md += [f"### {x['id']} — {x['severity'].upper()}: {x['problem']}",f"**Anchor:** PDF p{a['page']}, {a['section']}; `{a['tex_file']}:{a['line_range'][0]}–{a['line_range'][1]}`.",f"> {a['quoted_text']}",'',*x['reasoning_chain'],'',f"**Fix, only in a permitted revision window:** {x['fix']['instruction']}", '**Acceptance:** '+'; '.join(x['fix']['acceptance_criteria']),'']
md+=['## Every figure: visual inventory','','| Figure / PDF page | Source anchor | What is actually shown / assessment | Internal score |','|---|---|---|---:|']
for f in figs:
    a=f['location'];md.append(f"| {f['figure_id']} / p{f['page']} | `{a['tex_file']}:{a['line_range'][0]}` | {f['current_state']} {' '.join(f['problems'])} | {f['internal_quality_score']} |")
md+=['','Detailed figure crops: `renders/figure-01.png` through `figure-08.png`; complete method/downstream crops are `figure-02-complete.png`, `figure-04-complete.png`, with full p8 figure stack in `figures-05-07-complete.png`. Page renders preserve full captions when an individual detail crop ends mid-caption.','','## Cold-start and validation semantics','','Figure 2 is **correct about the comparator**: candidate validation risk 0.45 passes cold-start risk 0.60. The main method (source `sections/method.tex:69–85`, PDF p4) explicitly rejects higher-or-equal cold-start-relative error and otherwise retains the previous predicate. This is not a monotonic guarantee against the previous accepted predicate. Appendix G.1 (`sections/appendix/ablation_components.tex:29–31`, PDF p21) states that distinction and reports 262 retained decisions worse than the previous predicate. A compact main caveat would improve interpretation without alleging a diagram inconsistency.','','Figure 5 shows test trajectories, not validation curves; Figure 7 shows initialization versus optimized policies, not zero-shot generalization to unseen skills. The current main split description explicitly identifies held-out tasks with retained gold skills represented during training. The corrected replay definition/current-task inclusion, normalized ranking/tie handling, global split wording and fixed retriever setup are not treated as unresolved historical issues.','','## All-page coverage','','All pages were rendered at 108 dpi and inspected in eight contact sheets; all figure-bearing pages additionally received high-resolution detail inspection. Text extraction and page-boundary checks cover every page. This is presentation coverage, not a claim of independently reproducing every table or checking every citation.','','| Page | Content / inspection result |','|---:|---|']
for p in report['page_audit']:md.append(f"| {p['page']} | {p['topic']}. {p['finding']} |")
md+=['','## Verification and remaining inputs','',f"- Parsed figures from PDF captions: {figure_ids}; matches the eight-figure visual inventory.",f"- Checked {len(manifest)} immutable snapshot entries against `snapshot.json`: no mismatches.",f"- `pdffonts`: {len(font_records)} font records, all embedded; {report['acl_arr_compliance']['confirmed_physical_properties']['type3_records']} Type 3 records. Existing font-extraction warnings are not font-embedding findings.",'- All issue quotations are programmatically found in the cited source, with computed 1-based line anchors. Fixes are recommendations only; stage/permission remains unknown.','- Required human inputs: target/stage, actual AI use/checklist, submission logistics and supplements. No experiment or manuscript edit was needed for this audit.','', '**Files:** `presentation.json` (machine-readable source of truth), `presentation.md` (this report), `presentation_physical.json`, `pdffonts.txt`, page/text/figure renders and the two local audit/report scripts.']
(R/'presentation.md').write_text('\n'.join(md)+'\n')
print(json.dumps({'report_files':['presentation.json','presentation.md'],'pages':len(report['page_audit']),'figures':len(figs),'issues':len(issues),'severity_counts':dict(collections.Counter(x['severity'] for x in issues)),'font_records':len(font_records),'type3_records':report['acl_arr_compliance']['confirmed_physical_properties']['type3_records'],'manifest_entries':len(manifest),'snapshot_mismatches':changed,'json_parses':bool(json.loads((R/'presentation.json').read_text()))},indent=2))
